2026-10-22T14:15:07.4411658Z             "body": "## Summary\n\nComplete the Resources tab epic with shared background sampling, btop-style CPU/memory/disk/network panels, and an Agents pane that attributes local and remote coding-agent processes to sessions, tasks, or external origins. This rollup also includes the Resources configuration and GitBook guide.\n\nIssue #16 adds the live tmux E2E proof for all three harnesses, verifies external-agent attribution and panel controls, and measures sampler CPU with 1,000 processes. The sampler now requests executable and command metadata required to classify unregistered agents; bare `codex` processes are recognized as well.\n\n## Sub-issues and implementation PRs\n\nAll sub-issues were implemented on `senamakel/medulla:epic/15-resources`:\n\n- #1 — [PR #17](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/17)\n- #2 — [PR #35](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/35)\n- #3 — [PR #36](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/36)\n- #4 — [PR #40](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/40)\n- #5 — [PR #47](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/47)\n- #6 — [PR #48](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/48)\n- #7 — [PR #52](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/52)\n- #8 — [PR #53](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/53)\n- #9 — [PR #41](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/41)\n- #10 — [PR #55](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/55)\n- #11 — [PR #58](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/58)\n- #12 — [PR #59](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/59)\n- #13 — [PR #60](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/60)\n- #14 — [PR #61](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/61) and [follow-up PR #62](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/62)\n- #15 — [PR #63](https://github.com/senamakel/medulla/pull/63)\n- #16 — included on the epic branch at `9e9e528c18a00612efc954c9759f60debaf5d7ba`\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make ci` — passed (format, Clippy, locked tests, locked all-target build)\n- `make e2e-docker-all E2E_IMAGE=medulla-e2e:latest` — passed for OpenCode, Claude, and Codex\n- Classifier mutation proof — the focused tmux E2E failed at the exact external-PID assertion when OpenCode detection was removed; production source was restored\n- Resources performance — each harness stayed within the 40 ms/tick p95 and 2% one-core average limits with 1,000 processes over 60 seconds\n- Independent review — no actionable findings\n\nCloses #15\nCloses senamakel/medulla#16\n",
